    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Wrapper around a user functor. User code doesn&apos;t often use reference counting smart pointers for functors, but more often creates functors in global data or on the stack. The purpose of <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1CommandLine_1_1UserAction" kindref="compound">UserAction</ref> is to be a wrapper around these functors, to be a bridge between the world of reference counting pointers and objects or object references. For example, say the user has a function like this:</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">void<sp/>showRawManPage(const<sp/>ParserResult<sp/>*cmdline)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>std::cout<sp/>&lt;&lt;cmdline-&gt;parser()-&gt;manpage();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>exit(0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para><para>Then the functor/function can be used like this:</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">switchGroup.insert(Switch(&quot;raw-man&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>.action(userAction(showRawManPage))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>.doc(&quot;Prints<sp/>the<sp/>raw<sp/>nroff<sp/>man<sp/>page<sp/>to<sp/>standard<sp/>output.&quot;));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
